  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "We have only one data point (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA → 48.5% acc), so the dominant uncertainty is whether adding image modality provides complementary signal. Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the minimal logical extension of config_001: it keeps the same RNA encoder and profile setting and adds only the image branch with the simplest fusion (concat). This cleanly isolates the effect of multimodality. If accuracy improves meaningfully, subsequent budget can be directed at image encoder choice and fusion strategy; if it does not, we learn that image adds little and can focus on RNA encoder (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation instead. No other single experiment answers this highest-impact design question with fewer confounds."
}

